{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json\np=Path('/work/experiments/review_log.md')\np.write_text(p.read_text()+'''\n## Executed commands and outcomes\n\n- \"'`python3 /work/experiments/run_native_checks.py`: runs the exact DRC and netlist argv recorded in native_commands.json; both returned 0. Inspected independent_drc.json: zero violations, unconnected items and schematic parity issues. Native hashes before and after match the packet. No native connectivity defect established.\n- `python3 /work/experiments/inspect_physical.py`: independently tokenizes and reads entire native PCB and schematic, compares exported nets with supplied connectivity, extracts outline, pads, tracks, courtyard boxes and saved fill. Results in physical_inspection.json; generated saved_copper.png and visually inspected it. OUT T-junction is on the connected F.Cu segment, not an open end. C1 ground trace reaches the via; via is inside saved B.Cu polygon. Header ground thermal contacts occur diagonally.\n- First sampled ground path incorrectly attempted to enter the ground header on a cardinal thermal clearance and returned false; that was a bad probe path, not a native open circuit. Final path approaches along the saved diagonal spoke: all 1503 samples inside fill, including endpoint within J1.3'\"'s copper radius. Native DRC separately reports no open connection. Sampling is not a proof of continuous connectivity and is not an electrical impedance measurement.\n- Two exploratory \"'`/usr/bin/python3` pcbnew API probes called LoadBoard, GetConnectivity, GetConnectedPads and then BuildConnectivity. Before BuildConnectivity the direct connected-pad lists were empty; no inference made from unbuilt connectivity. Second probe stopped on a TypeError because GetUnconnectedCount requires a visibility argument. Discarded these probes for adjudication; relied on recorded native DRC and independent raw geometry. No board Save or refill call was made. The recurring three PROPERTY_ENUM assertions accompanied import, not native rule failures.\n- `python3 /work/experiments/calculate_response.py`: parses independent exported component values and records ideal unloaded assumptions and equations in response_calculation.json; generates nominal_baseline.cir. R1=10k, C1=100n, tau=1 ms, Vout(1 ms)=0.6321205588 V. The allowed tau interval for the same ideal initial condition and no load is 0.952542318 to 1.033501973 ms. This is not a component tolerance specification.\n- `ngspice -b /work/experiments/nominal_baseline.cir > /work/experiments/ngspice_baseline.log 2>&1`: returned 0; measured v_at_1ms=0.6321206 V. Stimulus is 0-to-1 V PWL with 1 ps rise, capacitor initially zero, maximum timestep 100 ns. Inspecting the measurement, not just the exit, confirms the stated nominal baseline. The hand-built ideal bench omits ADC and all extracted PCB parasitics, so cannot validate the loaded requirement.\n- Read versions.json and ngspice_baseline.log and located source values/pads/routes with `rg -n` and requirement with `nl -ba`. Python 3.12.3, KiCad 10.0.7, ngspice 42.\n\n## Assessment and coverage omissions\n\nNo evidence-supported saved-board geometry, placement or native-rule defect identified. Electrical acceptance with a switched ADC is indeterminate, recorded as a concern rather than a design failure. The source contains generic R/C footprints and nominal values, with no selected part datasheets or tolerance/temperature/bias models. Do not infer ratings from 0805 size or qualify current from 0.25 mm tracks. Geometry reviewed is the saved fill only; refill/fabrication exports and physical manufactured-board measurements were not performed. No specified fab capabilities, stackup copper thickness, part thermal ratings or operating environment were supplied, so no process or thermal qualification is claimed. No ECU requirements imposed.\n\nSpecific omissions: ADC capacitance, switch resistance, sampling instant/duration/repetition and sample capacitor prior voltage; source impedance/rise time and actual initial filter charge; real component tolerance/leakage/bias/temperature behavior; interconnect/connector/cable/return parasitics and resulting transient impedance; fabricated hardware and oscilloscope measurements; assembly/part-specific footprint validation, fab process capability and thermal measurements. Original ERC was reviewed but not rerun. Ignored native rules remain as listed in original ERC/DRC and the independent DRC output. No external references were fetched because no part models or externally specified ratings were used.\n'\"''')\nr=json.loads(Path('/work/experiments/independent_drc.json').read_text())\nprint({k:r[k] for k in ['ignored_checks','violations','unconnected_items','schematic_parity']})\nprint('Experiment files:', sorted(x.name for x in p.parent.iterdir() if x.is_file()))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
